openapi: 3.0.3

info:
  title: Breaker API
  version: 1.0.0
  contact:
    name: Breaker Support
    email: support@breaker.email
  description: |
    Use the Breaker API to manage campaigns, read your reporting, build
    segments and work with contacts from your own code.

    This is the public part of Breaker. Routes that the Breaker app uses
    internally are not part of this API and are not supported.

    ## Authentication

    Every request needs an API key, sent as a bearer token:

    ```bash
    curl https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/campaigns \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer bk_live_your_key_here"
    ```

    A key belongs to one newsletter. That is why no endpoint takes a newsletter
    ID. The key already says which newsletter you are working with. To work
    with more than one newsletter, create a key for each.

    Owners and admins create keys in the Breaker app under
    **Settings → API Keys**. The key is shown once, when you create it. Breaker
    stores only a hash of it, so a lost key cannot be recovered. Create a new
    key and revoke the old one.

    Treat a key like a password. Keep it on your server. Never put it in a
    browser, a mobile app, or a public repository. If a key leaks, revoke it in
    the app. Revocation takes effect straight away.

    ## Getting started

    Five calls that cover most integrations.

    **1. Create a draft campaign.**

    ```bash
    curl -X POST https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/campaigns \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $BREAKER_KEY" \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"title": "Weekly roundup", "subject": "Your week in review"}'
    ```

    The draft is created empty. This API cannot send campaigns. A person sends
    them from the Breaker app.

    **2. Write its body.**

    ```bash
    curl -X PUT https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/campaigns/4821/content \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $BREAKER_KEY" \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"html": "<h1 style=\"font-size:24px\">This week</h1>"}'
    ```

    Send an HTML fragment with the styles written into the elements. The
    endpoint below explains the rules.

    **3. List what you have.**

    ```bash
    curl "https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/campaigns?status=sent&pageSize=50" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $BREAKER_KEY"
    ```

    **4. Read a report.**

    ```bash
    curl "https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/reports/summary?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $BREAKER_KEY"
    ```

    **5. Find who clicked a link.**

    ```bash
    curl https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/campaigns/4821/links \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $BREAKER_KEY"

    curl https://api.breaker.email/v1/public/campaigns/4821/links/97/clicks \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $BREAKER_KEY"
    ```

    ## Using Breaker from an AI tool

    Breaker publishes an MCP server, [`@breaker-email/mcp`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@breaker-email/mcp),
    so Claude, Cursor, Codex and other AI tools can use this API in conversation.
    It covers the same endpoints documented here, runs on your own machine, and
    talks to Breaker with your API key. Nothing is sent anywhere except to Breaker.

    Create a key in Breaker at [app.breaker.email](https://app.breaker.email)
    under **Settings** then **API Keys**, then set the server up in your tool:

    - **Claude Code** — `claude mcp add breaker --scope user --env BREAKER_API_KEY=$BREAKER_KEY -- npx -y @breaker-email/mcp`
    - **Codex** — `codex mcp add breaker --env BREAKER_API_KEY=$BREAKER_KEY -- npx -y @breaker-email/mcp`
    - **Cursor** — add the config below to `~/.cursor/mcp.json`
    - **Claude Desktop** — **Settings**, **Developer**, **Edit Config**, then add the config below
    - **VS Code** — add the config below to your MCP config, under `servers` rather than `mcpServers`

    ```json
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "breaker": {
          "command": "npx",
          "args": ["-y", "@breaker-email/mcp"],
          "env": { "BREAKER_API_KEY": "bk_live_your_key_here" }
        }
      }
    }
    ```

    The [package page on npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@breaker-email/mcp)
    carries the same steps in more detail, along with a prompt you can paste into
    an AI assistant to have it do the setup for you.

    Web clients that connect to a URL rather than launching a program, such as
    claude.ai, use Breaker's hosted endpoint instead:

    ```text
    https://api.breaker.email/mcp
    ```

    Add it as a remote MCP server or connector and sign in with your Breaker
    account when the client asks. No API key is involved. The sign-in picks one
    newsletter, and the connection can be removed in the app under
    **Settings**, **Integrations**, **AI Clients**.

    Four things are deliberately not offered as tools, so an assistant cannot do
    them. Sending a campaign, which stays a decision a person makes in the app.
    Deleting a campaign or an automation, which cannot be undone. Creating a
    custom field, whose type is fixed at creation with no way to remove it
    afterwards. Switching an automation on is not in the API at all, for the
    same reason as sending.

    Everything else in this reference is available. Asking for a campaign to be
    drafted creates a draft and writes its body, leaving it for you to review and
    send. The same 60 requests a minute apply, shared with any other use of that
    key.

servers:
  - url: https://api.breaker.email/v1/public
    description: Production

security:
  - bearerAuth: []

tags:
  - name: Newsletter
    description: The newsletter your API key belongs to.
  - name: Campaigns
    description: Create, read and manage campaigns.
  - name: Automations
    description: |
      One triggered email per audience. An automation goes to every new contact
      who arrives through its audience: everyone, imports and manual adds, the
      prospecting drip, one signup form, or Zapier. A signup-form automation
      wins over the everyone automation for contacts from that form.

      Through this API you can draft an automation, write its body in the same
      HTML the campaign endpoints accept, and change its settings. It starts
      off, and stays off until a person turns it on in the app under
      **Automation**; `active` is read-only here. A newsletter can hold one
      automation per audience, and one per signup form, so a second one on the
      same audience is refused with the id of the one that already covers it.

      Contacts queue for an active automation the moment they are created and
      receive it within about ten minutes, once each. There is no reporting
      per automation.
  - name: Reports
    description: Delivery and engagement analytics, per campaign or over a date range.
  - name: Segments
    description: |
      Groups of contacts, either a fixed list or defined by rules. A segment
      is the audience a person picks when sending from the Breaker app. This
      API builds and reads segments and does not send.

      ### Building a dynamic segment

      1. Look up the IDs the rules will name: `GET /tags`, `GET /fields`,
         `GET /campaigns`, `GET /campaigns/{campaignId}/links` and
         `GET /signup-forms`. Never guess an ID.
      2. Call `POST /segments` with `type: "dynamic"` and `rules`. Leave out
         `contactIds` and `emails`.
      3. Read `contactCount` in the response. It is the real membership.
         Zero usually means an operator or value is wrong, not that nobody
         matches.

      A rule set is two levels deep, and both levels use `match`:

      ```json
      {
        "match": "all",
        "groups": [
          { "match": "all", "conditions": [ ] },
          { "match": "any", "conditions": [ ] }
        ]
      }
      ```

      `match: "all"` is AND. `match: "any"` is OR. The top-level `match`
      combines the groups, and each group's `match` combines its own
      conditions. For plain AND, use one `all` group. For "A and (B or C)",
      use `match: "all"` at the top, an `all` group holding A and an `any`
      group holding B and C. For "A or B", use one `any` group. The examples
      on `POST /segments` show each shape.

      Which condition kind to use:

      | You want contacts who... | `type` |
      | --- | --- |
      | opened, clicked or were sent any campaign in the last N days | `activity` |
      | opened, clicked or were sent one specific campaign | `campaign` |
      | carry or lack a tag | `tag` |
      | have a built-in field value, such as country or job title | `attribute` |
      | have a custom field value | `customField` |
      | subscribed through a specific signup form | `signupForm` |
      | subscribed, unsubscribed, last opened or last clicked before or after a date | `date` |
      | have a lifetime total or rate, such as open rate | `metric` |
      | ever clicked a URL matching a pattern | `linkClicked` |

      Every condition names its kind in `type` and carries only the fields
      that kind lists under `SegmentCondition`. `exists` and `doesNotExist`
      take no `value`. Dates are ISO 8601 with a time zone. Rates are 0 to
      100. One-line recipes for each kind are under `SegmentRuleSet`.

      ### Field reference

      What each condition kind takes. Operators in the `value` column that
      say "none" mean the condition carries no `value` at all.

      | `type` | Fields | Operators | `value` |
      | --- | --- | --- | --- |
      | `attribute`, text | `attribute`: any `ContactAttribute` except the three below | `is`, `isNot`, `contains`, `doesNotContain`, `startsWith`, `endsWith`, `exists`, `doesNotExist` | string up to 255 chars; none for `exists`, `doesNotExist` |
      | `attribute`, number | `attribute`: `companyEmployeeCount`, `companyEstimatedRevenue` | `equals`, `notEquals`, `greaterThan`, `greaterOrEqual`, `lessThan`, `lessOrEqual`, `exists`, `doesNotExist` | number; none for `exists`, `doesNotExist` |
      | `attribute`, provider | `attribute`: `emailProvider` | `is`, `isNot`, `exists`, `doesNotExist` | one of `EmailProvider`; none for `exists`, `doesNotExist` |
      | `customField`, `text` or `url` field | `fieldId` from `GET /fields` | the text operators above | string up to 1000 chars |
      | `customField`, `number` field | `fieldId` | the number operators above | number |
      | `customField`, `boolean` field | `fieldId` | `isTrue`, `isFalse`, `exists`, `doesNotExist` | none |
      | `customField`, `date` field | `fieldId` | `after`, `onOrAfter`, `before`, `onOrBefore`, `exists`, `doesNotExist` | ISO 8601 date-time; none for `exists`, `doesNotExist` |
      | `tag` | `tagId` from `GET /tags` | `has`, `doesNotHave` | none |
      | `signupForm` | `formId` from `GET /signup-forms` | `signedUp`, `didNotSignUp` | none |
      | `campaign` | `campaignId` from `GET /campaigns`; `linkId` from `GET /campaigns/{campaignId}/links`, only with `clickedLink` | `action`: `sent`, `opened`, `clicked`, `clickedLink` | none |
      | `linkClicked` | none | `is`, `isNot`, `contains`, `doesNotContain`, `startsWith`, `endsWith`, `exists` | the URL or part of it, up to 1000 chars; none for `exists` |
      | `date` | `event`: `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `unsubscribedAt`, `lastOpenedAt`, `lastClickedAt` | `after`, `onOrAfter`, `before`, `onOrBefore`, `exists`, `doesNotExist` | ISO 8601 date-time; none for `exists`, `doesNotExist` |
      | `metric` | `metric`: `totalSent`, `totalDelivered`, `totalOpens`, `uniqueOpens`, `totalClicks`, `uniqueClicks`, `openRate`, `uniqueOpenRate`, `clickRate`, `uniqueClickRate`, `totalRealClicks`, `uniqueRealClicks`, `realClickRate`, `uniqueRealClickRate` | `equals`, `notEquals`, `greaterThan`, `greaterOrEqual`, `lessThan`, `lessOrEqual` | number, required. Totals are campaign counts. Rates are 0 to 100. RealClick metrics exclude scanner clicks from 21 August 2026 onward |
      | `activity` | `activity`: `sent`, `opened`, `clicked`; `days`: 1 to 365 | `equals`, `notEquals`, `greaterThan`, `greaterOrEqual`, `lessThan`, `lessOrEqual`, default `greaterOrEqual` | `count`: how many campaigns in the window, 0 or more |

      How values are compared:

      - `exists` means the field is filled in. `doesNotExist` means it is
        empty. An empty field never matches `isNot`, `doesNotContain` or
        `notEquals`, so "country is not DE" leaves out contacts with no
        country. Add `doesNotExist` in an `any` group to include them.
      - Text comparison ignores case, so `country is de` matches `DE`.
        `contains`, `startsWith` and `endsWith` are substring matches.
      - `metric` values are never empty. A contact with no sending history
        counts as 0 on every metric, and a rate is opens or clicks divided by
        campaigns delivered, as a percentage capped at 100. The RealClick™
        metrics (`totalRealClicks`, `uniqueRealClicks`, `realClickRate`,
        `uniqueRealClickRate`) leave out automated scanner clicks, but only
        for clicks made on or after 21 August 2026; earlier clicks count as
        real. Their rates use the same delivered denominator.
      - `activity` counts campaigns whose event falls in the last `days`
        days, measured from now at recalculation time. `count: 0` with
        `equals` means "none in the window".
      - `campaign` with `clickedLink` needs `linkId`, and refuses it with any
        other action.
      - `linkClicked` with `exists` means "clicked any link in any campaign".
        There is no `doesNotExist`, since it would match nobody.
      - A `date` value is compared as an instant, so `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z`
        and `2026-01-01T02:00:00+02:00` are the same moment.
  - name: Contacts
    description: Contacts, their tags, custom fields and engagement.

paths:
  /newsletter:
    get:
      tags: [Newsletter]
      summary: The newsletter this key belongs to
      operationId: getNewsletter
      description: |
        The newsletter your API key is scoped to, with its ID and name. A key
        belongs to one newsletter, so this tells you which one you are working
        in without naming it yourself.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The newsletter.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Newsletter'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns:
    post:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Create a draft campaign
      operationId: createCampaign
      description: |
        Creates an empty draft campaign on your newsletter and returns it.

        The draft has no content. Write it with
        `PUT /campaigns/{campaignId}/content`, or open the returned `id` in the
        Breaker app. A draft created this way is identical to one created with
        the **New campaign** button.

        Sending is not part of this API. A person sends from the app.
      requestBody:
        required: false
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateCampaignRequest'
            examples:
              named:
                summary: Named draft
                value:
                  title: Weekly roundup, week 32
                  subject: Your week in review
              default:
                summary: Everything defaulted
                value: {}
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The created draft.
          headers:
            X-RateLimit-Limit:
              $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitLimit'
            X-RateLimit-Remaining:
              $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitRemaining'
            X-RateLimit-Reset:
              $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitReset'
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Campaign'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    get:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: List campaigns
      operationId: listCampaigns
      description: |
        Lists campaigns on your newsletter, newest first. Omit `status` to get
        every campaign regardless of status.
      parameters:
        - name: status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Return only campaigns with this status. Omit for all.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignStatus'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of campaigns.
          headers:
            X-RateLimit-Limit:
              $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitLimit'
            X-RateLimit-Remaining:
              $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitRemaining'
            X-RateLimit-Reset:
              $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitReset'
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns/{campaignId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'

    get:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Get a campaign
      operationId: getCampaign
      description: |
        Returns one campaign, including its HTML body and email settings.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The campaign.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignDetail'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    patch:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Update campaign settings
      operationId: updateCampaign
      description: |
        Updates the campaign's name, subject line or preview text. Send only
        the fields you want to change.

        This does not change campaign content. Use
        `PUT /campaigns/{campaignId}/content` for the body.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UpdateCampaignRequest'
            examples:
              subjectOnly:
                summary: Change the subject line
                value:
                  subject: A better subject line
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The updated campaign.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignDetail'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    delete:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Delete a draft campaign
      operationId: deleteCampaign
      description: |
        Deletes a campaign. **Drafts only.**

        A campaign in any other status returns `invalid_request`: deleting a
        sent campaign would destroy its reporting history, and this API cannot
        send campaigns, so it has no business deleting sends.
      responses:
        '204':
          description: Deleted. No body.
        '400':
          description: The campaign is not a draft.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
              example:
                error:
                  code: invalid_request
                  message: Only draft campaigns can be deleted
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns/{campaignId}/html:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'
    get:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Export the rendered email
      operationId: exportCampaignHtml
      description: |
        Returns the campaign as a complete HTML email, wrapped in the sending
        template with your newsletter's branding. This is close to what a
        subscriber receives, without per-recipient personalisation applied.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The rendered email.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignHtml'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns/{campaignId}/content:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'
    get:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Read the campaign body
      operationId: getCampaignContent
      description: |
        Returns the stored body, in exactly the shape `PUT` accepts back. An
        empty string means nothing has been written yet.

        This is the body on its own. `GET /campaigns/{campaignId}/html` returns
        the finished email, with the document wrapper, footer and unsubscribe
        block added. That version cannot be written back.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The stored body.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignContent'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'
    put:
      tags: [Campaigns]
      summary: Replace the campaign body
      operationId: updateCampaignContent
      description: |
        Replaces the campaign's body with the HTML you send.

        Send a fragment, not a whole document. Breaker adds the `<html>` and
        `<head>`, the preview text, your newsletter's footer and the
        unsubscribe link when the campaign sends.

        Write your styles into the elements, using `style` attributes. Breaker
        does not inline CSS for you, so a `<style>` block is passed through as
        it is and most inboxes ignore it. This is the most common reason
        generated HTML arrives looking unstyled.

        `mode` decides what the Breaker editor does with your HTML when someone
        opens the campaign later. The field description below covers both
        options.

        You can only write to a draft. A campaign that has been scheduled or
        sent is refused, because this API cannot send and does not rewrite what
        subscribers already received. Campaigns built in Breaker's earlier
        editor are also refused. Anything you create through this API works.

        ### Blocks the editor recognises

        In `adopt` mode the editor reads the fragment into its own blocks and
        keeps only the markup listed here. Anything else is unwrapped: its
        text survives, its layout and styling do not. A plain `<div>`,
        `<table>`, `<center>`, or `<span>` without a `style` attribute is
        unwrapped. A `<style>` element is dropped with its contents. Classes
        mean nothing except the three named below. To see the exact markup,
        read a campaign that was built in the app with
        `GET /campaigns/{campaignId}/content`.

        - **Paragraph**: `<p>`. Only `text-align` and a `font-size` of
          `12px`, `16px` or `18px` are kept. Other styles are replaced with
          the editor's own.
        - **Heading**: `<h1>` to `<h6>`. Only `text-align` is kept. Colour a
          heading with a `<span style="color:#...">` inside it.
        - **List**: `<ul>` or `<ol start="3">`, each `<li>` holding a `<p>`.
        - **Quote**: `<blockquote><p>...</p></blockquote>`.
        - **Divider**: `<hr>`, or
          `<div data-horizontal-rule="true" color="#E0E0E0" height="1" width="100"><hr></div>`
          to set the colour, the thickness in pixels and the width in
          percent. These are attributes, not styles.
        - **Button**:
          `<a data-custom-button="true" href="https://example.com" style="background-color:#111111;color:#ffffff;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;margin:15px auto">Read more</a>`.
          The label is the text. Only the style properties shown, plus
          `font-style` and `text-decoration`, are read. `margin:15px auto`
          centres the button, `15px auto 15px 0` puts it on the left and
          `15px 0 15px auto` on the right. Padding and corner radius are
          fixed.
        - **Image**:
          `<div class="image-component" style="text-align:center;padding-top:15px;padding-bottom:15px"><a href="https://example.com"><img src="https://example.com/hero.png" alt="Describe it" width="600" height="300"></a></div>`.
          The `<a>` is optional. `text-align` on the wrapper aligns the
          image and `padding-top` sets the space above it. A bare `<img>`
          works too, but loses its link. Give every image an `alt`, the app
          refuses to send without one. An image wider than the content area
          is scaled down.
        - **Columns**:
          `<table class="column-block"><tr><td class="column"><p>Left</p></td><td class="column"><p>Right</p></td></tr></table>`.
          Two or more cells, each `<td class="column">`, each holding any of
          the blocks in this list. Columns are always equal width. A `<td>`
          without the class is unwrapped.
        - **Custom HTML**: `<div data-type="custom-html">...</div>`. Kept
          byte for byte and never parsed, so this is where layout tables,
          `<style>` and anything else the editor does not know belong.
          `mode: preserve` wraps the whole body in one of these.
        - **Link preview card**:
          `<div data-type="custom-embed" data-url="https://example.com/post" data-title="Post title" data-image="https://example.com/og.png" data-description="One line" style="text-align:center"></div>`.
          The card is drawn from the data attributes, so the element can be
          empty. Leave `data-title` empty and the editor fetches the page's
          own title and image when it opens.
        - **Merge tag**: `<span class="merge-tag">{{contact-first-name}}</span>`,
          or `{{contact-first-name|there}}` with a fallback. The slug is the
          field key with underscores turned into dashes. Custom fields use
          their `key` from `GET /fields`. `{{date_MMMM D, YYYY}}` inserts the
          send date. Bare `{{...}}` text outside a span is still substituted
          when the campaign sends, but is not editable as a tag in the app.
        - **Inline formatting**: `<strong>`, `<em>`, `<u>`, `<s>`, `<code>`,
          `<a href>`, `<br>`, and
          `<span style="color:#ff0000;font-family:Georgia,serif;background-color:#ffff00">`
          for colour, font and highlight. A `font-size` on a span is dropped.

        RSS blocks are set up in the app and are best left alone.

        Email-wide settings are optional. Wrap the fragment in
        `<div data-bg-color="#f4f4f4" data-sheet-color="#ffffff" data-max-width="700" data-side-padding="24" data-line-height="1.5" data-paragraph-spacing="15"><div>...</div></div>`
        to set the background, the sheet colour, the width and side padding
        in pixels, the line height and the paragraph spacing in pixels. Line
        height and paragraph spacing apply to every paragraph. There is no
        per-block control of them.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UpdateCampaignContentRequest'
            examples:
              adopt:
                summary: Editable in Breaker afterwards
                value:
                  html: '<h1>This week</h1><p>Hi <span class="merge-tag">{{contact-first-name|there}}</span>, three things worth your time.</p><table class="column-block"><tr><td class="column"><h3>Read</h3><p>The long piece.</p></td><td class="column"><h3>Watch</h3><p>The short talk.</p></td></tr></table><hr><a data-custom-button="true" href="https://example.com/issue/32" style="background-color:#111111;color:#ffffff;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;margin:15px auto">Read the issue</a>'
              preserve:
                summary: Kept exactly as sent
                value:
                  html: '<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%"><tr><td align="center">Designed elsewhere</td></tr></table>'
                  mode: preserve
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The body as stored.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignContent'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /automations:
    get:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: List automations
      operationId: listAutomations
      description: |
        Every automation on the newsletter, newest first, on or off. Bodies are
        not included; use `GET /automations/{automationId}` for one.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of automations.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'
    post:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Create an automation
      operationId: createAutomation
      description: |
        Creates an automation with no body, switched off. Write the body with
        `PUT /automations/{automationId}/content`, then a person turns it on in
        the app.

        `audience` decides who receives it. `signupForm` needs the form's
        `signupFormId`, from `GET /signup-forms`; every other audience refuses
        one. A newsletter holds one automation per audience, and one per signup
        form, so a second on the same audience is refused with the id of the
        existing one.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateAutomationRequest'
            examples:
              everyone:
                summary: A welcome email for every new contact
                value:
                  name: Welcome
                  subject: Welcome aboard
                  previewText: Here is what to expect from us
                  audience: all
              signupForm:
                summary: For one signup form
                description: The form id comes from `GET /signup-forms`.
                value:
                  name: Webinar follow-up
                  subject: Your webinar recording
                  audience: signupForm
                  signupFormId: 9502
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The automation, with an empty body.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Automation'
        '400':
          description: A field is invalid, the form is unknown, or the audience is taken.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
              example:
                error:
                  code: invalid_request
                  message: Automation 12 already covers this audience. Update it, or delete it first
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /automations/{automationId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/AutomationId'
    get:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Get an automation
      operationId: getAutomation
      description: |
        Returns one automation's settings. The body is not included; read it
        with `GET /automations/{automationId}/content`.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The automation.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Automation'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'
    patch:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Update automation settings
      operationId: updateAutomation
      description: |
        Changes the name, subject line, preview text, audience or signup form.
        Send only the fields you want to change. Moving the audience off
        `signupForm` drops the form; moving it onto `signupForm` needs a
        `signupFormId` in the same request. The one-per-audience rule applies
        to the new audience.

        `active` cannot be set here. Switching an automation on is done by a
        person in the app. The body is written with
        `PUT /automations/{automationId}/content`.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UpdateAutomationRequest'
            examples:
              subjectOnly:
                summary: Change the subject line
                value:
                  subject: A warmer welcome
              moveToForm:
                summary: Tie it to one signup form
                value:
                  audience: signupForm
                  signupFormId: 9502
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The updated automation.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Automation'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'
    delete:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Delete an automation
      operationId: deleteAutomation
      description: |
        Deletes an automation, on or off, and drops any contacts still queued
        for it. There is no undo.
      responses:
        '204':
          description: Deleted. No body.
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /automations/{automationId}/content:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/AutomationId'
    get:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Read the automation body
      operationId: getAutomationContent
      description: |
        Returns the stored body, in exactly the shape `PUT` accepts back. An
        empty string means nothing has been written yet, and an automation with
        nothing written never sends, even when it is on.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The stored body.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationContent'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'
    put:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Replace the automation body
      operationId: updateAutomationContent
      description: |
        Replaces the automation's body with the HTML you send. The rules, the
        `mode` field and the block markup the editor recognises are exactly
        those of `PUT /campaigns/{campaignId}/content`; read that operation
        for the full reference.

        Unlike a campaign, an automation can be written at any time, on or
        off: the next contact to arrive receives the new body. Automations
        built in Breaker's earlier editor are refused.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UpdateCampaignContentRequest'
            examples:
              welcome:
                summary: A short welcome
                value:
                  html: '<h1>Welcome</h1><p>Hi <span class="merge-tag">{{contact-first-name|there}}</span>, thanks for joining. Here is what to expect.</p>'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The body as stored.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationContent'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /automations/{automationId}/html:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/AutomationId'
    get:
      tags: [Automations]
      summary: Preview the rendered body
      operationId: exportAutomationHtml
      description: |
        Returns the body as the send worker renders it, in the content table
        with your tracking parameters applied. An automation with no body
        returns `invalid_request`.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The rendered body.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationHtml'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /reports/summary:
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Aggregated stats over a date range
      operationId: getReportSummary
      description: |
        Totals across every campaign sent in the window, a per-day series, and
        the same totals for the preceding window of equal length so you can
        show a comparison.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/From'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/To'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Stats for the window.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportSummary'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /reports/campaigns/{campaignId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Stats for one campaign
      operationId: getCampaignReport
      description: |
        The same shape as the summary report, narrowed to a single campaign.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/From'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/To'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Stats for the campaign.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportSummary'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns/{campaignId}/interactions:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Per-contact engagement for a campaign
      operationId: listCampaignInteractions
      description: |
        One row per contact, with the times they opened, clicked, unsubscribed
        or complained. A `null` means the contact did not do that thing.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
        - name: sortBy
          in: query
          required: false
          schema:
            type: string
            enum:
              [
                openedAt,
                clickedAt,
                unsubscribedAt,
                spamComplainedAt,
                latestEventAt,
                email,
                firstName,
              ]
            default: openedAt
        - name: sortDirection
          in: query
          required: false
          schema:
            type: string
            enum: [asc, desc]
            default: desc
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of interactions.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/InteractionList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns/{campaignId}/links:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Clicks per link
      operationId: listCampaignLinks
      description: |
        Every link in the campaign with its click counts. `realClicks` excludes
        clicks attributed to security scanners, which is usually the number you
        want to report.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The campaign's links.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LinkList'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /campaigns/{campaignId}/links/{linkId}/clicks:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/CampaignId'
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/LinkId'
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Contacts who clicked a link
      operationId: listLinkClicks
      description: |
        The contacts who clicked one specific link, and when. Use this to build
        an audience from what people were interested in.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of clicks.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/LinkClickList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /reports/subscribers:
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Current subscriber count
      operationId: getSubscriberCount
      description: |
        How many contacts are currently subscribed to your newsletter.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The count.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SubscriberCount'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /reports/unsubscribes:
    get:
      tags: [Reports]
      summary: Unsubscribes over a date range
      operationId: getUnsubscribes
      description: |
        How many contacts unsubscribed in the window, with a per-day series.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/From'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/To'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Unsubscribes for the window.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/UnsubscribeReport'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /segments:
    get:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: List segments
      operationId: listSegments
      description: |
        Every segment on your newsletter, static and rule-driven.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of segments.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    post:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: Create a segment
      operationId: createSegment
      description: |
        Creates a segment, either from a fixed list of contacts or from rules.

        **Static** (`type: "static"`, the default): identify contacts by
        `contactIds`, by `emails`, or both. Addresses that do not match a
        contact on your newsletter are skipped rather than failing the request,
        and the response reports how many were matched.

        **Dynamic** (`type: "dynamic"`): supply `rules` instead of contacts.
        Membership is computed straight away from every subscribed contact, so
        the `contactCount` in the response is the segment's real size. The
        rule format is described under `SegmentRuleSet`. Every tag, custom
        field, campaign, link and signup form a rule names must belong to your
        newsletter, or the request fails with `invalid_request` naming the ID
        that does not.

        A dynamic segment can be opened and edited in the Breaker app like any
        other, and its rules can be replaced later with
        `PUT /segments/{segmentId}/rules`.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateSegmentRequest'
            examples:
              byEmail:
                summary: Static, from a list of addresses
                value:
                  name: Webinar attendees
                  emails: [ada@example.com, grace@example.com]
              byId:
                summary: Static, from contact IDs
                value:
                  name: VIPs
                  contactIds: [1201, 1202]
              dynamicAnd:
                summary: 'Dynamic, plain AND: one all group'
                description: |
                  Opened at least 2 campaigns in the last 30 days and carries
                  tag 12. Both conditions must hold, so they sit in one `all`
                  group.
                value:
                  name: Engaged VIPs
                  type: dynamic
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: all
                        conditions:
                          - type: activity
                            activity: opened
                            days: 30
                            operator: greaterOrEqual
                            count: 2
                          - type: tag
                            tagId: 12
                            operator: has
              dynamicOr:
                summary: 'Dynamic, plain OR: one any group'
                description: |
                  Signed up through form 9502 or ever clicked a pricing link.
                  Either is enough, so they sit in one `any` group.
                value:
                  name: Pricing interest
                  type: dynamic
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: any
                        conditions:
                          - type: signupForm
                            formId: 9502
                            operator: signedUp
                          - type: linkClicked
                            operator: contains
                            value: /pricing
              dynamicMixed:
                summary: 'Dynamic, A and (B or C): two groups'
                description: |
                  In Germany and opened something this month, and either
                  tagged 12 or clicked campaign 4821. The `all` group holds
                  the must-haves, the `any` group holds the alternatives, and
                  the top-level `match: all` requires both groups.
                value:
                  name: Engaged in Germany
                  type: dynamic
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: all
                        conditions:
                          - type: attribute
                            attribute: country
                            operator: is
                            value: DE
                          - type: activity
                            activity: opened
                            days: 30
                            operator: greaterOrEqual
                            count: 1
                      - match: any
                        conditions:
                          - type: tag
                            tagId: 12
                            operator: has
                          - type: campaign
                            campaignId: 4821
                            action: clicked
              dynamicWinBack:
                summary: 'Dynamic, exclusion: subscribers gone quiet'
                description: |
                  Subscribed before 1 June 2026 and opened nothing in the last
                  90 days. There is no "not" on a group, so absence is an
                  `activity` count of exactly 0.
                value:
                  name: Win-back
                  type: dynamic
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: all
                        conditions:
                          - type: date
                            event: createdAt
                            operator: before
                            value: '2026-06-01T00:00:00Z'
                          - type: activity
                            activity: opened
                            days: 90
                            operator: equals
                            count: 0
              dynamicCustomField:
                summary: 'Dynamic, custom field and metric'
                description: |
                  Custom field 44 (from `GET /fields`, a text field) contains
                  "pro" and the lifetime open rate is 20% or more.
                value:
                  name: Pro plan readers
                  type: dynamic
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: all
                        conditions:
                          - type: customField
                            fieldId: 44
                            operator: contains
                            value: pro
                          - type: metric
                            metric: openRate
                            operator: greaterOrEqual
                            value: 20
      responses:
        '201':
          description: |
            The created segment. A static segment also reports what the
            contacts you supplied resolved to; a dynamic one is the plain
            segment, with `contactCount` set to what its rules matched.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                oneOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentWithMembership'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Segment'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /segments/{segmentId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/SegmentId'
    get:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: Get a segment
      operationId: getSegment
      description: |
        One segment with its settings and current contact count.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The segment.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Segment'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /segments/{segmentId}/rules:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/SegmentId'
    get:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: Get a segment's rules
      operationId: getSegmentRules
      description: |
        The rules defining a dynamic segment, in the same format
        `POST /segments` and `PUT /segments/{segmentId}/rules` accept, so a
        segment can be read, adjusted and written back. Static segments return
        `null`.

        A segment built in the Breaker app may use a condition this API does
        not express. Such a condition comes back as `type: "unsupported"` with
        the stored node in `raw`, and it is kept as-is if you write the rules
        back with the unsupported condition included.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The rules, or null for a static segment.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentRules'
              examples:
                dynamic:
                  summary: A dynamic segment
                  value:
                    segmentId: 310
                    rules:
                      match: all
                      groups:
                        - match: all
                          conditions:
                            - type: activity
                              activity: opened
                              days: 30
                              operator: greaterOrEqual
                              count: 2
                            - type: tag
                              tagId: 12
                              operator: has
                static:
                  summary: A static segment
                  value:
                    segmentId: 311
                    rules: null
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    put:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: Replace a dynamic segment's rules
      operationId: replaceSegmentRules
      description: |
        Replaces the rules of a dynamic segment and recalculates its
        membership straight away. The response is the segment with the
        `contactCount` the new rules produce.

        The whole rule set is replaced, not merged: read the current rules
        first if you want to change one condition. Static segments return
        `invalid_request`, since their membership is a fixed list.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentRulesRequest'
            examples:
              recentSubscribers:
                summary: Subscribed this year and never unsubscribed
                value:
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: all
                        conditions:
                          - type: date
                            event: createdAt
                            operator: onOrAfter
                            value: '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'
                          - type: date
                            event: unsubscribedAt
                            operator: doesNotExist
              keepUnsupported:
                summary: Tighten a segment built in the app, keeping what the API cannot express
                description: |
                  Read with `GET /segments/{segmentId}/rules`, an extra
                  condition added, written back. The `unsupported` node came
                  from the read and is passed through unchanged.
                value:
                  rules:
                    match: all
                    groups:
                      - match: all
                        conditions:
                          - type: unsupported
                            raw:
                              id: 5f1c2a6e-8d3b-4c2f-9a41-0b7e6d2c1f33
                              typ: dfield
                              xid: contact_status
                              op: '='
                              comp: sub
                          - type: activity
                            activity: clicked
                            days: 60
                            operator: greaterOrEqual
                            count: 1
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The segment after recalculation.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Segment'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /segments/{segmentId}/contacts:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/SegmentId'
    get:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: List contacts in a segment
      operationId: listSegmentContacts
      description: |
        The contacts currently in the segment. For a dynamic segment this is
        the membership as of the last recalculation.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of contacts.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    post:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: Add contacts to a static segment
      operationId: addSegmentContacts
      description: |
        Adds contacts to a static segment, by ID or email. Contacts already in
        the segment are left alone, so this is safe to call repeatedly with
        overlapping lists.

        Dynamic segments return `invalid_request`: their membership comes from
        their rules, not from a list.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentContactsRequest'
            examples:
              byEmail:
                summary: By address
                value:
                  emails: [ada@example.com]
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Membership after the change.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentWithMembership'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /segments/{segmentId}/recalculate:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/SegmentId'
    post:
      tags: [Segments]
      summary: Recalculate a dynamic segment
      operationId: recalculateSegment
      description: |
        Re-runs a dynamic segment's rules and refreshes its membership. Static
        segments return `invalid_request`, since there is nothing to
        recalculate.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: |
            The segment after recalculation. `contactCount` is the membership
            the rules now produce.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Segment'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /contacts:
    post:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Create a contact
      operationId: createContact
      description: |
        Adds a contact to your newsletter.

        Custom fields are addressed by their key, which you can list with
        `GET /fields`. Unknown keys return `invalid_request` rather than being
        silently dropped, and so do tag IDs that belong to another newsletter:
        a request is either applied in full or refused.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateContactRequest'
            examples:
              minimal:
                summary: Just an address
                value:
                  email: ada@example.com
              full:
                summary: With fields and tags
                value:
                  email: ada@example.com
                  firstName: Ada
                  lastName: Lovelace
                  customFields:
                    plan: pro
                  tagIds: [12]
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The created contact.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Contact'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '403':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Forbidden'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: List contacts
      operationId: listContacts
      description: |
        Contacts on your newsletter, newest first.

        Filter by `email` to look up the ID for an address you already know,
        which is how most integrations start.
      parameters:
        - name: email
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Exact address match. Returns at most one contact.
          schema:
            type: string
            format: email
          example: ada@example.com
        - name: status
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Return only contacts with this status.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactStatus'
        - name: tagId
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Return only contacts carrying this tag.
          schema:
            type: integer
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of contacts.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactList'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /contacts/{contactId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ContactId'
    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Get a contact
      operationId: getContact
      description: One contact with its fields and tags.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The contact.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Contact'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    patch:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Update a contact
      operationId: updateContact
      description: |
        Updates standard fields, custom fields, or both. Send only what you
        want to change. Fields you leave out are not touched.

        All changes in one request are applied together. If any field fails
        validation, none of them are written.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UpdateContactRequest'
            examples:
              fields:
                summary: Name and a custom field
                value:
                  firstName: Ada
                  customFields:
                    plan: enterprise
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The updated contact.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Contact'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /contacts/{contactId}/tags/{tagId}:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ContactId'
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/TagId'
    post:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Tag a contact
      operationId: tagContact
      description: |
        Adds a tag to a contact. Adding a tag the contact already has succeeds
        and changes nothing.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The contact, with its tags.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Contact'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    delete:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Remove a tag from a contact
      operationId: untagContact
      description: |
        Removes a tag. Removing a tag the contact does not have succeeds and
        changes nothing.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The contact, with its tags.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Contact'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /contacts/{contactId}/status:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ContactId'
    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Get a contact's subscription status
      operationId: getContactStatus
      description: |
        Whether the contact is subscribed, and when that last changed.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The status.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactStatusDetail'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /contacts/{contactId}/analytics:
    parameters:
      - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ContactId'
    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Get a contact's engagement
      operationId: getContactAnalytics
      description: |
        How this contact has engaged across campaigns: what they were sent,
        what they opened, and which links they clicked.
      parameters:
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Page'
        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/PageSize'
      responses:
        '200':
          description: A page of per-campaign engagement.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactAnalytics'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '404':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/NotFound'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /tags:
    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: List tags
      operationId: listTags
      description: |
        Every tag on your newsletter. You need these IDs to tag a contact.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The tags.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/TagList'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    post:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Create a tag
      operationId: createTag
      description: Creates a tag. Names must be unique on a newsletter.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateTagRequest'
            examples:
              basic:
                summary: A new tag
                value:
                  name: Webinar 2026
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The created tag.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Tag'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /fields:
    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: List custom fields
      operationId: listFields
      description: |
        The custom fields defined on your newsletter, with the key you use to
        set them on a contact.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The custom fields.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/FieldList'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

    post:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: Create a custom field
      operationId: createField
      description: |
        Defines a new custom field. The `type` fixes what values the field
        accepts and cannot be changed afterwards.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateFieldRequest'
            examples:
              text:
                summary: A text field
                value:
                  name: Plan
                  type: text
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The created field.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Field'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

  /signup-forms:
    get:
      tags: [Contacts]
      summary: List signup forms
      operationId: listSignupForms
      description: |
        The signup forms on your newsletter, as built under **Growth** in the
        Breaker app. You need a form's `id` for a `signupForm` segment rule,
        which matches contacts by the form they subscribed through.
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The signup forms.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/SignupFormList'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'
        '429':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/RateLimited'
        '500':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/InternalError'

components:
  securitySchemes:
    bearerAuth:
      type: http
      scheme: bearer
      description: |
        An API key created in the Breaker app under **Settings → API Keys**,
        sent as `Authorization: Bearer bk_live_...`. Each key is scoped to a
        single newsletter.

  parameters:
    CampaignId:
      name: campaignId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Campaign ID.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      example: 4821
    AutomationId:
      name: automationId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Automation ID.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      example: 77
    SegmentId:
      name: segmentId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Segment ID.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      example: 310
    ContactId:
      name: contactId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Contact ID.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      example: 1201
    TagId:
      name: tagId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Tag ID.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      example: 12
    LinkId:
      name: linkId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Link ID, from the campaign's links report.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
      example: 97
    Page:
      name: page
      in: query
      required: false
      description: 1-indexed page number.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
        default: 1
    PageSize:
      name: pageSize
      in: query
      required: false
      description: Items per page.
      schema:
        type: integer
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 100
        default: 20
    From:
      name: from
      in: query
      required: true
      description: First day of the window, inclusive, UTC.
      schema:
        type: string
        format: date
      example: '2026-08-01'
    To:
      name: to
      in: query
      required: true
      description: Last day of the window, inclusive, UTC.
      schema:
        type: string
        format: date
      example: '2026-08-31'

  headers:
    XRateLimitLimit:
      description: Requests allowed per window.
      schema:
        type: integer
        example: 60
    XRateLimitRemaining:
      description: Requests left in the current window.
      schema:
        type: integer
        example: 59
    XRateLimitReset:
      description: Unix timestamp (seconds) when the window resets.
      schema:
        type: integer
        example: 1756400460
    RetryAfter:
      description: Seconds to wait before retrying.
      schema:
        type: integer
        example: 30

  schemas:
    Newsletter:
      type: object
      description: |
        The newsletter an API key belongs to. Identity only: enough to tell two
        keys apart, and to name what you are working in.
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 318
        name:
          type: string
          example: My Weekly Digest
      required: [id, name]

    CampaignStatus:
      type: string
      description: The delivery state of a campaign.
      enum: [draft, scheduled, sending, sent, paused, failed]

    ContactStatus:
      type: string
      description: Whether a contact receives campaigns.
      enum: [subscribed, unsubscribed, pending, suppressed]

    Pagination:
      type: object
      properties:
        totalItems:
          type: integer
          description: Items matching the query, across all pages.
          example: 137
        totalPages:
          type: integer
          example: 7
        currentPage:
          type: integer
          example: 1
        pageSize:
          type: integer
          example: 20
      required: [totalItems, totalPages, currentPage, pageSize]

    CreateCampaignRequest:
      type: object
      description: Every field is optional. Send `{}` to create a default draft.
      properties:
        title:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
          default: Draft Campaign
          description: Internal name, shown in the campaigns list. Not visible to subscribers.
          example: Weekly roundup, week 32
        subject:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
          description: Email subject line. Can be left empty and set later.
          example: Your week in review
      additionalProperties: false

    UpdateCampaignRequest:
      type: object
      description: Send only the fields you want to change. At least one is required.
      minProperties: 1
      properties:
        title:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
        subject:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
        previewText:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
          nullable: true
          description: The preview line shown after the subject in most inboxes.
      additionalProperties: false

    Campaign:
      type: object
      description: A campaign, as returned in lists.
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          description: Campaign ID. Use it to open the campaign in the app.
          example: 4821
        title:
          type: string
          description: Internal name.
          example: Weekly roundup, week 32
        status:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignStatus'
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          description: When the campaign was created (ISO 8601, UTC).
          example: '2026-08-28T09:14:22Z'
        scheduledAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
          description: |
            When the campaign is scheduled to send, or was sent (ISO 8601,
            UTC). `null` for a draft.
          example: '2026-09-01T13:00:00Z'
      required: [id, title, status, createdAt, scheduledAt]

    CampaignDetail:
      allOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Campaign'
        - type: object
          properties:
            subject:
              type: string
              description: Email subject line.
              example: Your week in review
            previewText:
              type: string
              nullable: true
              description: Preview line shown after the subject.
            content:
              type: string
              nullable: true
              description: |
                The campaign body as HTML. `null` for a draft with nothing
                written yet. This is the body only. Use
                `GET /campaigns/{campaignId}/html` for the full rendered email.
          required: [subject, previewText, content]

    CampaignHtml:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 4821
        html:
          type: string
          description: The complete email, wrapped in your sending template.
      required: [id, html]

    CampaignContent:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 4821
        html:
          type: string
          description: |
            The stored body, in the same form that `PUT` accepts. Empty when
            nothing has been written yet. If the body was sent with
            `mode: preserve`, this includes the wrapper element that Breaker
            puts around your markup.
      required: [id, html]

    UpdateCampaignContentRequest:
      type: object
      properties:
        html:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          description: |
            The campaign body, as an HTML fragment. Maximum 5 MB.

            Breaker adds `<!DOCTYPE>`, `<html>`, `<head>` and `<body>` when the
            campaign sends, so sending them here is refused. `<script>` elements
            and inline event handlers such as `onclick` are refused as well.
            Everything else is stored exactly as you sent it.
        mode:
          type: string
          enum: [adopt, preserve]
          default: adopt
          description: |
            What the Breaker editor should do with this HTML when someone opens
            the campaign.

            `adopt` stores the HTML as you wrote it. The editor reads it into
            its own blocks, so the campaign stays editable in the normal way.
            Headings, paragraphs, images and links all become real editor
            content. Markup the editor does not recognise is changed or dropped,
            and opening the campaign can save that changed version back over
            what you sent. Use this when a person will finish the draft in
            Breaker.

            `preserve` keeps your markup exactly as it is, inside a single HTML
            block. It reaches the inbox unchanged. In the editor it shows up as
            one block that can only be edited as raw HTML, and editing it there
            applies Breaker's list of allowed tags. Use this for templates
            designed outside Breaker.
      required: [html]
      additionalProperties: false

    CampaignList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Campaign'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [data, pagination]

    AutomationAudience:
      type: string
      description: |
        Who receives the automation. `all` is every new contact. `imported` is
        contacts added by import or by hand. `prospecting` is the prospecting
        drip. `signupForm` is one signup form, named by `signupFormId`.
        `zapier` is contacts created through Zapier.
      enum: [all, imported, prospecting, signupForm, zapier]

    Automation:
      type: object
      description: An automation's settings. The body is served by the content route.
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 77
        name:
          type: string
          description: Internal name. Subscribers never see it.
          example: Welcome
        subject:
          type: string
          description: Email subject line.
          example: Welcome aboard
        previewText:
          type: string
          nullable: true
          description: Preview line shown after the subject.
        audience:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationAudience'
        signupFormId:
          type: integer
          nullable: true
          description: The form, for a `signupForm` audience. `null` otherwise.
          example: null
        active:
          type: boolean
          description: |
            Whether new contacts receive it. Read-only: a person switches it
            on or off in the app.
          example: false
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          example: '2026-09-01T10:00:00Z'
        updatedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          example: '2026-09-02T10:00:00Z'
      required: [id, name, subject, previewText, audience, signupFormId, active, createdAt, updatedAt]

    AutomationList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Automation'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [data, pagination]

    AutomationContent:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 77
        html:
          type: string
          description: |
            The stored body, in the same form that `PUT` accepts. Empty when
            nothing has been written yet.
      required: [id, html]

    AutomationHtml:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 77
        html:
          type: string
          description: The body as the send worker renders it.
      required: [id, html]

    CreateAutomationRequest:
      type: object
      properties:
        name:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
          description: Internal name. Subscribers never see it.
          example: Welcome
        subject:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
          example: Welcome aboard
        previewText:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
          nullable: true
          description: The preview line shown after the subject in most inboxes.
        audience:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationAudience'
        signupFormId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          nullable: true
          description: |
            Required for the `signupForm` audience, from `GET /signup-forms`.
            Refused for every other audience.
      required: [name, subject, audience]
      additionalProperties: false

    UpdateAutomationRequest:
      type: object
      description: Send only the fields you want to change. At least one is required.
      minProperties: 1
      properties:
        name:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
        subject:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
        previewText:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
          nullable: true
        audience:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AutomationAudience'
        signupFormId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          nullable: true
          description: |
            Only with the `signupForm` audience, in the same request or already
            set. Refused for every other audience.
      additionalProperties: false

    ReportTotals:
      type: object
      description: Counts for a window. Every field is a whole number.
      properties:
        recipients:
          type: integer
          description: |
            Contacts the campaigns in scope were sent to, counted over the whole
            life of those campaigns rather than only this window. On a campaign
            report that is the campaign's own send size. On the summary it is
            every campaign in the newsletter. Every other figure here is limited
            to the window, so use `delivered` when you want a like-for-like
            comparison.
          example: 12480
        delivered:
          type: integer
          description: Emails accepted by the receiving server.
          example: 12310
        opensTotal:
          type: integer
          example: 8422
        opensUnique:
          type: integer
          description: Distinct contacts who opened.
          example: 5104
        clicksTotal:
          type: integer
          example: 1930
        clicksUnique:
          type: integer
          description: Distinct contacts who clicked.
          example: 1201
        realClicksTotal:
          type: integer
          description: |
            Clicks with automated scanner traffic removed. Only counted for
            campaigns sent after this feature shipped, so historical windows
            may report 0 here while `clicksTotal` is non-zero.
          example: 1602
        realClicksUnique:
          type: integer
          description: Distinct contacts, scanner traffic removed.
          example: 1044
        unsubscribes:
          type: integer
          example: 37
        softBounces:
          type: integer
          example: 22
        hardBounces:
          type: integer
          example: 9
        spamComplaints:
          type: integer
          example: 3
      required:
        - recipients
        - delivered
        - opensTotal
        - opensUnique
        - clicksTotal
        - clicksUnique
        - realClicksTotal
        - realClicksUnique
        - unsubscribes
        - softBounces
        - hardBounces
        - spamComplaints

    DailyPoint:
      type: object
      properties:
        date:
          type: string
          format: date
          example: '2026-08-14'
        delivered:
          type: integer
        opensTotal:
          type: integer
        opensUnique:
          type: integer
        clicksTotal:
          type: integer
        clicksUnique:
          type: integer
        unsubscribes:
          type: integer
      required: [date, delivered, opensTotal, opensUnique, clicksTotal, clicksUnique, unsubscribes]

    ReportSummary:
      type: object
      description: |
        Totals for the window you asked for, the same totals for the preceding
        window of equal length, and a day-by-day series.
      properties:
        from:
          type: string
          format: date
          example: '2026-08-01'
        to:
          type: string
          format: date
          example: '2026-08-31'
        totals:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportTotals'
        previousPeriod:
          type: object
          description: |
            The window of the same length immediately before yours, for
            comparison. For 1 to 31 August, this is 1 to 31 July.
          properties:
            from:
              type: string
              format: date
              example: '2026-07-01'
            to:
              type: string
              format: date
              example: '2026-07-31'
            totals:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportTotals'
          required: [from, to, totals]
        daily:
          type: array
          description: One entry per day in the window, including days with no activity.
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/DailyPoint'
      required: [from, to, totals, previousPeriod, daily]

    Interaction:
      type: object
      description: |
        One contact's engagement with a campaign. A `null` timestamp means the
        contact did not do that thing.
      properties:
        contactId:
          type: integer
          example: 1201
        email:
          type: string
          format: email
          example: ada@example.com
        firstName:
          type: string
          nullable: true
          example: Ada
        lastName:
          type: string
          nullable: true
          example: Lovelace
        openedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
        clickedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
        unsubscribedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
        spamComplainedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
      required: [contactId, email, openedAt, clickedAt, unsubscribedAt, spamComplainedAt]

    InteractionList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Interaction'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [data, pagination]

    Link:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          description: Use this with the link clicks endpoint.
          example: 97
        url:
          type: string
          nullable: true
          example: https://example.com/pricing
        clicksTotal:
          type: integer
          example: 412
        clicksUnique:
          type: integer
          example: 318
        realClicksTotal:
          type: integer
          description: Scanner traffic removed. See the note on report totals.
          example: 355
      required: [id, url, clicksTotal, clicksUnique, realClicksTotal]

    LinkList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Link'
      required: [data]

    LinkClick:
      type: object
      properties:
        contactId:
          type: integer
          example: 1201
        email:
          type: string
          format: email
          example: ada@example.com
        clickedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          example: '2026-08-14T11:02:41Z'
      required: [contactId, email, clickedAt]

    LinkClickList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/LinkClick'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [data, pagination]

    SubscriberCount:
      type: object
      properties:
        subscribers:
          type: integer
          description: Contacts currently subscribed.
          example: 12480
      required: [subscribers]

    UnsubscribeReport:
      type: object
      properties:
        from:
          type: string
          format: date
        to:
          type: string
          format: date
        total:
          type: integer
          example: 37
        daily:
          type: array
          items:
            type: object
            properties:
              date:
                type: string
                format: date
              unsubscribes:
                type: integer
            required: [date, unsubscribes]
      required: [from, to, total, daily]

    Segment:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 310
        name:
          type: string
          example: Webinar attendees
        description:
          type: string
          nullable: true
        type:
          type: string
          description: |
            `static` is a fixed list of contacts. `dynamic` is defined by rules
            and recalculated.
          enum: [static, dynamic]
        contactCount:
          type: integer
          description: Contacts currently in the segment.
          example: 842
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
      required: [id, name, description, type, contactCount, createdAt]

    SegmentList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Segment'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [data, pagination]

    SegmentWithMembership:
      allOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Segment'
        - type: object
          properties:
            matchedContacts:
              type: integer
              description: |
                How many of the contacts you supplied were found on your
                newsletter and are now in the segment.
              example: 2
            unmatchedEmails:
              type: array
              description: |
                Addresses that did not match a contact and were skipped. Empty
                when everything matched.
              items:
                type: string
                format: email
          required: [matchedContacts, unmatchedEmails]

    SegmentRules:
      type: object
      description: The rules of a dynamic segment, or `null` for a static one.
      properties:
        segmentId:
          type: integer
          example: 310
        rules:
          nullable: true
          allOf:
            - $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentRuleSet'
      required: [segmentId, rules]

    SegmentRulesRequest:
      type: object
      properties:
        rules:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentRuleSet'
      required: [rules]
      additionalProperties: false

    SegmentRuleSet:
      type: object
      description: |
        What a contact must satisfy to be in a dynamic segment.

        A rule set is groups of conditions. Within a group, `match: all` means
        every condition must hold and `match: any` means at least one must.
        The groups are then combined the same way by the rule set's own
        `match`. So "in Germany and opened something this month, and either
        tagged VIP or clicked campaign 4821" is one `all` rule set holding an
        `all` group and an `any` group.

        Only subscribed contacts are considered: a contact who unsubscribes
        leaves the segment at the next recalculation whatever the rules say.

        Up to 10 groups of up to 15 conditions each. Every condition names its
        kind in `type`; the kinds and what each needs are listed under
        `SegmentCondition`.

        Common recipes, each as one condition:

        - Opened at least 2 campaigns in the last 30 days:
          `{"type":"activity","activity":"opened","days":30,"operator":"greaterOrEqual","count":2}`
        - Opened nothing in the last 90 days:
          `{"type":"activity","activity":"opened","days":90,"operator":"equals","count":0}`
        - Never opened any campaign:
          `{"type":"metric","metric":"uniqueOpens","operator":"equals","value":0}`
        - Open rate of 20% or more:
          `{"type":"metric","metric":"openRate","operator":"greaterOrEqual","value":20}`
        - Clicked at least once, scanner clicks excluded:
          `{"type":"metric","metric":"uniqueRealClicks","operator":"greaterOrEqual","value":1}`
        - Subscribed since 1 January 2026:
          `{"type":"date","event":"createdAt","operator":"onOrAfter","value":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"}`
        - Carries tag 12:
          `{"type":"tag","tagId":12,"operator":"has"}`
        - Signed up through form 9502:
          `{"type":"signupForm","formId":9502,"operator":"signedUp"}`
        - Clicked campaign 4821:
          `{"type":"campaign","campaignId":4821,"action":"clicked"}`
        - Ever clicked a link to your pricing page:
          `{"type":"linkClicked","operator":"contains","value":"/pricing"}`
        - In Germany:
          `{"type":"attribute","attribute":"country","operator":"is","value":"DE"}`
        - Custom field 44 contains "pro":
          `{"type":"customField","fieldId":44,"operator":"contains","value":"pro"}`

        There is no "not" on a group. To exclude, use the negative operator
        of the condition: `doesNotHave`, `didNotSignUp`, `isNot`,
        `doesNotExist`, or an `activity` count of 0.
      example:
        match: all
        groups:
          - match: all
            conditions:
              - type: activity
                activity: opened
                days: 30
                operator: greaterOrEqual
                count: 2
          - match: any
            conditions:
              - type: tag
                tagId: 12
                operator: has
              - type: campaign
                campaignId: 4821
                action: clicked
      properties:
        match:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RuleMatch'
        groups:
          type: array
          minItems: 1
          maxItems: 10
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentRuleGroup'
      required: [match, groups]
      additionalProperties: false

    RuleMatch:
      type: string
      description: '`all` means every item must hold; `any` means at least one must.'
      enum: [all, any]

    SegmentRuleGroup:
      type: object
      properties:
        match:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RuleMatch'
        conditions:
          type: array
          minItems: 1
          maxItems: 15
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentCondition'
      required: [match, conditions]
      additionalProperties: false

    SegmentCondition:
      description: |
        One test on a contact. The `type` says which kind, and each kind has
        its own fields:

        - `attribute` — a built-in contact or company field, such as
          `country` or `companyName`.
        - `customField` — one of your custom fields, by the `id` from
          `GET /fields`. The operators that apply depend on the field's type.
        - `tag` — whether the contact carries a tag, by the `id` from
          `GET /tags`.
        - `signupForm` — whether the contact subscribed through a signup
          form, by the `id` from `GET /signup-forms`.
        - `campaign` — whether the contact was sent, opened or clicked a
          campaign, by the `id` from `GET /campaigns`; or clicked one
          specific link in it, by the `id` from `GET /campaigns/{campaignId}/links`.
        - `linkClicked` — whether the contact ever clicked a link whose URL
          matches, across every campaign.
        - `date` — when something happened to the contact: created, updated,
          unsubscribed, last opened, last clicked.
        - `metric` — the contact's lifetime totals and rates.
        - `activity` — how many campaigns the contact was sent, opened or
          clicked in the last N days.
        - `unsupported` — only ever returned, never accepted on its own: a
          condition built in the Breaker app that this API does not express.
          Write it back unchanged to keep it.
      oneOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/AttributeCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CustomFieldCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/TagCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/SignupFormCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/CampaignCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/LinkClickedCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/DateCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/MetricCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ActivityCondition'
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/UnsupportedCondition'
      discriminator:
        propertyName: type
        mapping:
          attribute: '#/components/schemas/AttributeCondition'
          customField: '#/components/schemas/CustomFieldCondition'
          tag: '#/components/schemas/TagCondition'
          signupForm: '#/components/schemas/SignupFormCondition'
          campaign: '#/components/schemas/CampaignCondition'
          linkClicked: '#/components/schemas/LinkClickedCondition'
          date: '#/components/schemas/DateCondition'
          metric: '#/components/schemas/MetricCondition'
          activity: '#/components/schemas/ActivityCondition'
          unsupported: '#/components/schemas/UnsupportedCondition'

    TextOperator:
      type: string
      description: |
        Operators on text. `exists` and `doesNotExist` test whether the value
        is set at all and take no `value`; the rest compare against `value`.
      enum: [is, isNot, contains, doesNotContain, startsWith, endsWith, exists, doesNotExist]

    NumberOperator:
      type: string
      description: |
        Operators on numbers. `exists` and `doesNotExist` test whether the
        value is set at all and take no `value`.
      enum:
        [
          equals,
          notEquals,
          greaterThan,
          greaterOrEqual,
          lessThan,
          lessOrEqual,
          exists,
          doesNotExist,
        ]

    ComparisonOperator:
      type: string
      description: Operators on a number that is always present, such as a total.
      enum: [equals, notEquals, greaterThan, greaterOrEqual, lessThan, lessOrEqual]

    DateOperator:
      type: string
      description: |
        Operators on a date. `exists` and `doesNotExist` test whether the event
        has happened at all and take no `value`.
      enum: [after, onOrAfter, before, onOrBefore, exists, doesNotExist]

    BooleanOperator:
      type: string
      description: Operators on a true/false custom field. None takes a `value`.
      enum: [isTrue, isFalse, exists, doesNotExist]

    ContactAttribute:
      type: string
      description: |
        The built-in fields of a contact. All are text and take `TextOperator`,
        except `companyEmployeeCount` and `companyEstimatedRevenue`, which are
        numbers and take `NumberOperator`, and `emailProvider`, which takes
        `is`, `isNot`, `exists` or `doesNotExist` with a value from
        `EmailProvider`.
      enum:
        - email
        - emailProvider
        - firstName
        - lastName
        - phone
        - jobTitle
        - linkedinProfile
        - country
        - state
        - city
        - streetAddress1
        - streetAddress2
        - postalCode
        - companyName
        - companyWebsite
        - companyIndustry
        - companyEmployeeCount
        - companyEstimatedRevenue
        - companyCountry
        - companyState
        - companyCity
        - companyStreetAddress1
        - companyStreetAddress2
        - companyPostalCode
        - utmSource
        - utmMedium
        - utmCampaign
        - utmTerm
        - utmContent

    EmailProvider:
      type: string
      description: The mail provider Breaker detected behind a contact's address.
      enum:
        - google
        - microsoft
        - yahoo
        - icloud
        - zoho
        - fastmail
        - yandex
        - mail.ru
        - comcast
        - charter
        - cox
        - att
        - verizon
        - godaddy
        - rackspace
        - amazon
        - sendgrid
        - mailgun
        - sparkpost
        - postmark
        - mailchimp
        - mimecast
        - proofpoint
        - barracuda
        - cisco
        - sophos
        - messagelabs
        - other

    AttributeCondition:
      type: object
      description: A test on a built-in contact or company field.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [attribute]
        attribute:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactAttribute'
        operator:
          type: string
          description: A `TextOperator`, or a `NumberOperator` for the two numeric attributes.
          example: is
        value:
          description: |
            Text for text attributes, a number for the numeric ones, an
            `EmailProvider` for `emailProvider`. Omit for `exists` and
            `doesNotExist`.
          oneOf:
            - type: string
              maxLength: 255
            - type: number
      required: [type, attribute, operator]
      additionalProperties: false
      example:
        type: attribute
        attribute: country
        operator: is
        value: DE

    CustomFieldCondition:
      type: object
      description: |
        A test on one of your custom fields. Which operators apply follows the
        field's type from `GET /fields`: `text` and `url` take `TextOperator`,
        `number` takes `NumberOperator`, `boolean` takes `BooleanOperator`, and
        `date` takes `DateOperator` with an ISO 8601 `value`.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [customField]
        fieldId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          example: 44
        operator:
          type: string
          example: contains
        value:
          description: |
            Text for text and url fields, a number for number fields, an ISO
            8601 date-time for date fields. Omit for boolean fields and for
            `exists` and `doesNotExist`.
          oneOf:
            - type: string
              maxLength: 1000
            - type: number
      required: [type, fieldId, operator]
      additionalProperties: false
      example:
        type: customField
        fieldId: 44
        operator: contains
        value: pro

    TagCondition:
      type: object
      description: Whether the contact carries a tag.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [tag]
        tagId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          example: 12
        operator:
          type: string
          enum: [has, doesNotHave]
      required: [type, tagId, operator]
      additionalProperties: false

    SignupFormCondition:
      type: object
      description: Whether the contact subscribed through a signup form.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [signupForm]
        formId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          example: 9502
        operator:
          type: string
          enum: [signedUp, didNotSignUp]
      required: [type, formId, operator]
      additionalProperties: false

    CampaignCondition:
      type: object
      description: |
        Whether the contact was sent, opened or clicked one campaign, or
        clicked one specific link in it. `linkId` is required for
        `clickedLink` and must be a link of that campaign; it is not accepted
        with any other action.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [campaign]
        campaignId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          example: 4821
        action:
          type: string
          enum: [sent, opened, clicked, clickedLink]
        linkId:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          example: 97
      required: [type, campaignId, action]
      additionalProperties: false

    LinkClickedCondition:
      type: object
      description: |
        Whether the contact ever clicked a link whose URL matches, in any
        campaign. `exists` means "clicked any link at all" and takes no
        `value`; `doesNotExist` is not offered, since every contact who
        clicked nothing would match nothing useful.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [linkClicked]
        operator:
          type: string
          enum: [is, isNot, contains, doesNotContain, startsWith, endsWith, exists]
        value:
          type: string
          maxLength: 1000
          description: The URL, or part of it. Omit for `exists`.
      required: [type, operator]
      additionalProperties: false
      example:
        type: linkClicked
        operator: contains
        value: /pricing

    DateCondition:
      type: object
      description: When something happened to the contact.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [date]
        event:
          type: string
          description: |
            `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are the contact record; the other three
            are when the contact last unsubscribed, opened and clicked.
          enum: [createdAt, updatedAt, unsubscribedAt, lastOpenedAt, lastClickedAt]
        operator:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/DateOperator'
        value:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          description: ISO 8601. Omit for `exists` and `doesNotExist`.
      required: [type, event, operator]
      additionalProperties: false
      example:
        type: date
        event: createdAt
        operator: onOrAfter
        value: '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'

    MetricCondition:
      type: object
      description: |
        The contact's lifetime engagement. Totals are counts of campaigns;
        rates are percentages from 0 to 100, opens or clicks over campaigns
        delivered. A contact with no history counts as 0.

        The RealClick™ metrics (`totalRealClicks`, `uniqueRealClicks`,
        `realClickRate`, `uniqueRealClickRate`) leave out automated inbox
        scanner clicks, but only for clicks made on or after 21 August 2026;
        earlier clicks count as real. Their rates divide by campaigns
        delivered like every other rate: `realClickRate` uses total
        RealClicks™, `uniqueRealClickRate` unique RealClicks™.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [metric]
        metric:
          type: string
          enum:
            - totalSent
            - totalDelivered
            - totalOpens
            - uniqueOpens
            - totalClicks
            - uniqueClicks
            - openRate
            - uniqueOpenRate
            - clickRate
            - uniqueClickRate
            - totalRealClicks
            - uniqueRealClicks
            - realClickRate
            - uniqueRealClickRate
        operator:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ComparisonOperator'
        value:
          type: number
          minimum: 0
      required: [type, metric, operator, value]
      additionalProperties: false
      example:
        type: metric
        metric: openRate
        operator: greaterOrEqual
        value: 20

    ActivityCondition:
      type: object
      description: |
        How many campaigns the contact was sent, opened or clicked in the last
        `days` days. "Opened at least twice in the last 30 days" is
        `activity: opened`, `days: 30`, `operator: greaterOrEqual`, `count: 2`.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [activity]
        activity:
          type: string
          enum: [sent, opened, clicked]
        days:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
          maximum: 365
          example: 30
        operator:
          allOf:
            - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ComparisonOperator'
          default: greaterOrEqual
        count:
          type: integer
          minimum: 0
          example: 2
      required: [type, activity, days, count]
      additionalProperties: false

    UnsupportedCondition:
      type: object
      description: |
        A condition built in the Breaker app that this API does not express.
        Returned as-is so nothing is hidden; include it unchanged when writing
        the rules back to keep it, or leave it out to drop it. It cannot be
        built from scratch here.
      properties:
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [unsupported]
        raw:
          type: object
          description: The stored condition, in the segment builder's own format.
          additionalProperties: true
      required: [type, raw]
      additionalProperties: false

    CreateSegmentRequest:
      type: object
      description: |
        A static segment takes `contactIds`, `emails`, or both, and at least
        one contact must match. A dynamic segment takes `rules` and neither
        contacts nor addresses.
      properties:
        name:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
          example: Webinar attendees
        type:
          type: string
          description: '`static` is a fixed list of contacts; `dynamic` is defined by `rules`.'
          enum: [static, dynamic]
          default: static
        description:
          type: string
          maxLength: 1000
        contactIds:
          type: array
          description: Static segments only.
          items:
            type: integer
            minimum: 1
        emails:
          type: array
          description: Static segments only.
          items:
            type: string
            format: email
        rules:
          allOf:
            - $ref: '#/components/schemas/SegmentRuleSet'
          description: Dynamic segments only, and required for them.
      required: [name]
      additionalProperties: false

    SegmentContactsRequest:
      type: object
      description: Supply `contactIds`, `emails`, or both.
      properties:
        contactIds:
          type: array
          items:
            type: integer
            minimum: 1
        emails:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
            format: email
      additionalProperties: false

    Contact:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 1201
        email:
          type: string
          format: email
          example: ada@example.com
        firstName:
          type: string
          nullable: true
        lastName:
          type: string
          nullable: true
        status:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactStatus'
        customFields:
          type: object
          description: Custom field values, keyed by field key.
          additionalProperties:
            type: string
            nullable: true
          example:
            plan: pro
        tagIds:
          type: array
          items:
            type: integer
          example: [12]
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
      required: [id, email, firstName, lastName, status, customFields, tagIds, createdAt]

    ContactList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Contact'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [data, pagination]

    CreateContactRequest:
      type: object
      properties:
        email:
          type: string
          format: email
        firstName:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
        lastName:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
        customFields:
          type: object
          description: Values keyed by custom field key. Unknown keys are rejected.
          additionalProperties:
            type: string
            nullable: true
        tagIds:
          type: array
          items:
            type: integer
            minimum: 1
      required: [email]
      additionalProperties: false

    UpdateContactRequest:
      type: object
      description: Send only what changes. At least one field is required.
      minProperties: 1
      properties:
        firstName:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
          nullable: true
        lastName:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
          nullable: true
        customFields:
          type: object
          additionalProperties:
            type: string
            nullable: true
      additionalProperties: false

    ContactStatusDetail:
      type: object
      properties:
        contactId:
          type: integer
        status:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactStatus'
        unsubscribedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
          description: When the contact unsubscribed, if they have.
      required: [contactId, status, unsubscribedAt]

    ContactCampaignEngagement:
      type: object
      properties:
        campaignId:
          type: integer
          example: 4821
        campaignTitle:
          type: string
        sentAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
        openedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
        clickedAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          nullable: true
        clickedUrls:
          type: array
          description: Links this contact clicked in this campaign.
          items:
            type: string
      required: [campaignId, campaignTitle, sentAt, openedAt, clickedAt, clickedUrls]

    ContactAnalytics:
      type: object
      properties:
        contactId:
          type: integer
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ContactCampaignEngagement'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
      required: [contactId, data, pagination]

    Tag:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 12
        name:
          type: string
          example: Webinar 2026
        contactCount:
          type: integer
          description: Contacts currently carrying this tag.
          example: 842
      required: [id, name, contactCount]

    TagList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Tag'
      required: [data]

    CreateTagRequest:
      type: object
      properties:
        name:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
      required: [name]
      additionalProperties: false

    Field:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 44
        key:
          type: string
          description: |
            Use this key when setting the field on a contact. It is derived from
            the name: lowercased, with every run of non-alphanumeric characters
            replaced by an underscore, so "Job Title" is `job_title`. Renaming a
            field in the app therefore changes its key, while the `id` does not
            change. Read the key from here rather than deriving it yourself.
          example: plan
        name:
          type: string
          example: Plan
        type:
          type: string
          description: What values the field accepts. Fixed at creation.
          enum: [text, number, boolean, date, url]
      required: [id, key, name, type]

    FieldList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Field'
      required: [data]

    CreateFieldRequest:
      type: object
      properties:
        name:
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
        type:
          type: string
          enum: [text, number, boolean, date, url]
      required: [name, type]
      additionalProperties: false

    SignupForm:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: integer
          example: 9502
        name:
          type: string
          description: The form's title as set in the Breaker app.
          example: Homepage footer
        style:
          type: string
          description: '`mini` is the email field and button; `full` adds the logo and a heading.'
          enum: [mini, full]
        signupCount:
          type: integer
          description: Contacts who subscribed through this form.
          example: 128
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
      required: [id, name, style, signupCount, createdAt]

    SignupFormList:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/SignupForm'
      required: [data]

    Error:
      type: object
      properties:
        error:
          type: object
          properties:
            code:
              type: string
              description: Stable, machine-readable code. Branch on this.
              enum:
                - invalid_request
                - unauthorized
                - invalid_api_key
                - newsletter_blocked
                - not_found
                - rate_limited
                - internal_error
            message:
              type: string
              description: Human-readable explanation. Do not parse.
            details:
              type: array
              description: |
                Present on validation failures that involve specific fields.
              items:
                type: object
                properties:
                  field:
                    type: string
                    example: email
                  message:
                    type: string
                    example: is not a valid email address
                required: [field, message]
          required: [code, message]
      required: [error]

  responses:
    BadRequest:
      description: A parameter is missing or malformed.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
          example:
            error:
              code: invalid_request
              message: pageSize must be between 1 and 100

    Unauthorized:
      description: The key is missing, unknown, or revoked.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
          example:
            error:
              code: invalid_api_key
              message: This API key is not valid

    Forbidden:
      description: This newsletter is currently blocked.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
          example:
            error:
              code: newsletter_blocked
              message: This newsletter cannot create campaigns right now

    NotFound:
      description: |
        No such resource on your newsletter. Returned both when the ID does not
        exist and when it belongs to another newsletter.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
          example:
            error:
              code: not_found
              message: No campaign with that ID

    RateLimited:
      description: Rate limit exceeded.
      headers:
        Retry-After:
          $ref: '#/components/headers/RetryAfter'
        X-RateLimit-Limit:
          $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitLimit'
        X-RateLimit-Remaining:
          $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitRemaining'
        X-RateLimit-Reset:
          $ref: '#/components/headers/XRateLimitReset'
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
          example:
            error:
              code: rate_limited
              message: Rate limit exceeded. Retry in 30 seconds

    InternalError:
      description: Something went wrong on our side.
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
          example:
            error:
              code: internal_error
              message: Something went wrong. Try again later
